oes not bar full formal discipline of a member who tenders a letter of resignation.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga23_1995__ci02.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Voluntary association principle applied to individual church membership","year":1991,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.md:occ-35d02633a507","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB affirmed that the principle of voluntary association governing churches also applies to individuals joining a local PCA congregation.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Voluntary resignation from membership and application of BCO 46-5","year":1991,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.md:occ-a6556e9299b6","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The GA clarified that BCO 46-5 had been variously interpreted regarding voluntary resignation, resolving that a simple resignation does not automatically trigger the willful-neglect excommunication process.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga19_1991__ci02.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Membership status and session authority upon dissolution of a congregation","year":1988,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.md:occ-86a9cf0ab384","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"Upon dissolution of a congregation, the session terminates, membership in the visible church is dissolved for those not transferred, and Presbytery may not unilaterally assign members to other churches.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether a resignation letter constitutes willful neglect justifying roll erasure","year":1988,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.md:occ-a15652ace64a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB held that 'deletion' under BCO 46-5 is equivalent to excommunication and referred the question of easier non-judicial removal to the 17th GA for potential BCO amendment.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga16_1988__ci09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Procedure for removing members who relocate without affiliating elsewhere","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.md:occ-c60b1c398bd7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"BCO 46-2 governs removal of members who move away and fail to affiliate within a year; BCO 46-5's formal discipline applies only to willful neglect, not mere relocation.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci10.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Teaching elder voting rights and congregational approval of pastoral salary changes","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.md:occ-8193d3066238","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB advised that a teaching elder votes as a full session member, and that any change to pastoral salary terms requires congregational approval as part of the call.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci11.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether deletion from the roll under BCO 46-5 constitutes excommunication","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.md:occ-6f533fcdae8d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB answered yes — 'deletion' under BCO 46-5 is excommunication in effect, and the due-process procedures of BCO 27-5 must therefore be followed.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether deletion from the roll under BCO 46-5 constitutes excommunication","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.md:occ-204cc68521f9","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB answered yes — 'deletion' under BCO 46-5 is excommunication in effect, and the due-process procedures of BCO 27-5 must therefore be followed.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci20.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Meaning of willful neglect and gross crime under BCO 46-5 and 30-4","year":1985,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.md:occ-144ede7fcf55","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"BCO 46-5 requires due process under BCO 27-5 for incorrigible members, and 'gross crime or heresy' is to be understood in its biblical and moral sense as determined by the church court.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci06.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David L. Thoburn v. Potomac Presbytery","year":1995,"disposition":"Partially","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.md:occ-087596d646a8","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":194},"excerpt":"The third avenue is in BCO 46-5. This section provides:","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga23_1995__1993-13.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1993-13"],"body":"SJC/CJB"}},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Chen v. Ascension Presbytery","year":1994,"disposition":"out_of_order","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-9eb71c8ee13e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":102},"excerpt":"…Savior is urged to consider deleting their names from the church roll under BCO 46-5 as requested by the Chens in their letter of April 26, 1992.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-f04250d2b7a5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":106},"excerpt":"### RESPONDENT PRESBYTERY OF THE ASCENSION AND THE SESSION OF THE CHURCH OF THE SAVIOR MISINTERPRETED BOOK OF CHURCH ORDER 46-5.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-33798f5dacb5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":112},"excerpt":"…the General Assembly made clear the proper constitutional interpretation of Book of Church Order 46- 5 as adopted at the 18th General Assembly (1990). Carl Fox tendered his letter of resignation to his Session which accepted it and removed his name from…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-a1432b822caa","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":112},"excerpt":"…name from the roll. The General Assembly said that was constitutional under BCO 46-5. On April 26, 1992, Dr. Chen wrote a letter to the Session of the Church of the Savior in response to a suggestion by a Ruling Elder (ROC p. 51). In this letter he stated…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-7966e0e86e84","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":124},"excerpt":"…The reason the Respondent Presbytery of the Ascension gave for not following BCO 46-5 was that the Chens' request \"was unbiblical and unconstitutional\" (Respondent's Brief page 3, para. 8) and to do so would be \"unconstitutional and therefore not…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-a4a4d667e44b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":124},"excerpt":"…We further conclude that it certainly meets one of the conditions set out in BCO 46-5, i.e. \"when a member... has made it known that he or she has no intention of fulfilling the church vows.\" But instead of granting Dr. Chen's request to \"simply remove our…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-dcf7926bb4ac","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":124},"excerpt":"…suspended them from the sacraments. We think the Session should have followed BCO 46-5 which states that under this condition \"then the Session should delete such names from the church rolls...\" The reason the Respondent Presbytery of the Ascension gave for…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md:occ-54a3598b981c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":126},"excerpt":"We believe this conclusion is the result of a misinterpretation of BCO 46-5 in view of the clarification of BCO 46-5 in the revision thereof finally adopted by the 18th General Assembly (1990) (M18GA pp 42-43).","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1993-3"],"body":"SJC"}},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Hathaway v. Grace Presbytery","year":1991,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md:occ-61466ed00e02","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":75},"excerpt":"3. Did the Commission err in this application of the procedure prescribed by BCO 46-5?","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md:occ-47c695669149","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":143},"excerpt":"…Waynesboro Presbyterian Church could be served by delaying the enforcement of BCO 46-5.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md:occ-a351d00bf391","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":171},"excerpt":"After individual pastoral ministry to several members of the Waynesboro Presbyterian Church had been unsuccessful in restoring them to active participation, and under the procedures of Book of Church Order 46-5, which states:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md"},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md:occ-fa5799a14e73","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":191},"excerpt":"…action on a recommendation of the pastor (complainant) that the procedures of Book of Church Order 46-5 be followed regarding certain members of the church. (p. 31, circled numbers in the Record)","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["church discipline","non-attending members","member roll deletion","session authority","pastoral duty","circularization of court","record of case","session discretion","absent members","neglect of church attendance","deletion from roll","complaint procedure","circularization of commission"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1990-9"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Vaughn Hathaway complained that the Session of Waynesboro Presbyterian Church failed to institute discipline against seven members who had not attended worship for over a year. The judicial panel denied the complaint on the grounds that the Session retained discretion to determine the timing of discipline proceedings, and procedural errors did not result in material prejudice."}},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Melton et al. v. Tennessee Valley Presbytery","year":1991,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.md:occ-884d3042368c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["proxy voting","congregational meeting","church dissolution","property transfer","secret ballot","Robert's Rules of Order","congregational vote","higher court authority over local church","complaint","presbytery action","local church"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1990-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Complainants challenged the ruling of the session of Westminster Presbyterian Church (Chattanooga) disallowing proxy votes at a December 10, 1989 congregational meeting that voted not to rescind the earlier dissolution and property transfer to New City Fellowship. The SJC denied all specifications, holding that proxy voting was not required under BCO 24-4 or Robert's Rules, and that the congregation's decision to dissolve was within its rights under BCO Chapter 25."}},{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"DeBardeleben v. Philadelphia Presbytery","year":1989,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga17_1989__case3.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--case:cases/ga17_1989__case3.md:occ-bf75ab605e4c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga17_1989__case3.html","repository_path":"cases/ga17_1989__case3.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":158},"excerpt":"- **g.** He proposed erasing the names of those who lost the vote on Feb. 4, 1987 from the roll of the church without due process. (cf. BCO 46-5)","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga17_1989__case3.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["judicial commission","trial de novo","church division","ministerial discipline","censure"],"case_numbers":["1988-6"],"body":"CJB","synopsis":"A complaint challenged Philadelphia Presbytery’s approval of proceedings that cleared teaching and ruling elders without properly trying serious public accusations arising from Christ Church’s division. All three specifications were sustained because plea bargaining, dropped charges, and failure to hear necessary witnesses left the accusations unresolved. Presbytery’s action was annulled and de novo trials produced mixed convictions and acquittals. Harold Burkhart received six months’ suspension, Douglas McCready an admonition, and six former ruling elders three-month suspensions. The decision stressed taking such conflicts to Presbytery or judicial process rather than the congregation."}},{"id":"bco:46-5--overture:ga24_1996:16","record_id":"overture:ga24_1996:16","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 46-5 by Substituting Alternative A","year":1996,"disposition":"Answered by reference","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga24_1996.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga24_1996.md","evidence_basis":"title_subject_reference","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:46-5--overture:ga24_1996:16:occ-1b40c7031cc1","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga24_1996.html#ga24-p54","repository_path":"mar